5. **Strict finite-grid maximum principle** (the required one):
```lean
theorem strict_finite_grid_max_principle {N : ℕ} (u : ℕ → ℝ)
    (hsub : ∀ i, 0 < i → i < N → u i < (u (i - 1) + u (i + 1)) / 2) :
    ∀ i, 0 < i → i < N → u i < max (u 0) (u N) := by
  classical
  intro i hi0 hiN
  by_contra hle
  push_neg at hle   -- hle : max (u 0) (u N) ≤ u i
  obtain ⟨k, -, hkmax⟩ := Finset.exists_max_image (Finset.range (N + 1)) u (Finset.range_nonempty (N + 1))
  -- hkmax : ∀ x' ∈ range (N+1), u x' ≤ u k
  have hk0 : k ≠ 0 := by
    rintro rfl
    have h0 : u i ≤ u 0 := hkmax i (Finset.mem_range.mpr (Nat.lt_succ_of_le (le_of_lt hiN)))
    linarith [le_max_left (u 0) (u N)]
  have hkN : k ≠ N := by
    rintro rfl
    have hN : u i ≤ u N := hkmax i (Finset.mem_range.mpr (Nat.lt_succ_of_le (le_of_lt hiN)))
    linarith [le_max_right (u 0) (u N)]
  have hkpos : 0 < k := Nat.pos_of_ne_zero hk0
  have hklt : k < N := lt_of_le_of_ne (Nat.lt_succ_iff.mp (Finset.mem_range.mp (Finset.mem_of_mem ... ))) hkN
```
Wait I need k ∈ range (N+1) from `Finset.exists_max_image` gives ⟨k, hk_mem, hkmax⟩. Then k ≤ N. And k ≠ N gives k < N. Good.

Then hsub k hkpos hklt: `u k < (u (k-1) + u (k+1))/2`.
Also hkmax gives u (k-1) ≤ u k since k-1 ∈ range(N+1) (k-1 ≤ k ≤ N < N+1), and u (k+1) ≤ u k since k+1 ≤ N < N+1 (using k < N). Then `(u(k-1)+u(k+1))/2 ≤ u k`. linarith finishes. 

Note: `push_neg at hle` turns `¬ u i < max...` into `max... ≤ u i`. Then `hkmax i ...` gives `u i ≤ u k`, so `u k ≥ u i ≥ max...`. Then contradiction: `u k < (u(k-1)+u(k+1))/2 ≤ u k`. linarith with facts: hsub k ..., hkmax (k-1) ..., hkmax (k+1) ..., hle, and `Nat.sub_add_cancel`? Wait hsub k uses `u (k - 1)`; with Nat subtraction fine since 0 < k. `k+1` is Nat addition.

But careful: `hkmax (k-1) (mem_range.mpr ...)` where `k-1 < N+1` — from k ≤ N, k-1 ≤ N < N+1. `omega` can prove. Similarly k+1 < N+1 from k < N.

